# The visual mode.

=== v and d delete the selection (inclusive)
text:
|abcdef
keys: vlld
want:
|def

=== v backwards
text:
abc|def
keys: vhhd
want:
a|ef

=== V deletes lines
text:
one
|two
three
four
keys: Vjd
want:
one
|four

=== y in the visual mode yanks
text:
|foo bar
keys: veyP
want:
fo|ofoo bar
mode: vim/normal

=== o goes to the other end
text:
ab|cdef
keys: vllohd
want:
a|f

=== c in the visual mode
text:
|foo bar
keys: vecbaz<Esc>
want:
ba|z bar

=== iw in the visual mode
text:
foo b|ar baz
keys: viwd
want:
foo | baz

=== gv selects again
text:
|abcdef
keys: vl<Esc>$gvd
want:
|cdef

=== Esc leaves without changing
text:
|abc
keys: vl<Esc>
want:
a|bc
mode: vim/normal

=== U and u change case
text:
|abc def
keys: veU
want:
|ABC def

=== > shifts the lines
text:
|one
two
keys: Vj>
want:
	|one
	two

=== J joins the lines
text:
|a
b
c
keys: VjjJ
want:
a b| c

=== p replaces the selection
text:
|one two
keys: yiwwviwp
want:
one on|e

=== a block deletes columns
text:
|abcd
efgh
ijkl
keys: <C-v>jjld
want:
|cd
gh
kl

=== a block yank and P
text:
|ab
cd
keys: <C-v>jyx
want:
|b
cd

=== dot repeats a visual delete of lines
text:
|1
2
3
4
5
keys: Vjd.
want:
|5
